{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What is special about our Game? </strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>It's very hard.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i> but also...</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>... a true Deckbuilding experience</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Darkest Cube, copying a deck list from the internet won\u2019t save you \u2014 every run begins with a unique seed, generating new relics, cards, and enemies each time. Strategy is everything: study your upcoming foes and adapt your deck to counter their strengths. Every card matters \u2014 even one you haven\u2019t used for hours might become the key to survival. And don\u2019t stick to just one archetype; sometimes, success means shifting from defensive to offensive or experimenting with effect-heavy builds. Adapt or perish.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3650350/extras/0d4c5e92cb271b02ebe2079999c81a03.avif?t=1770890325\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>... Rogue-like cycles, but in a RPG world?! Let's introduce you to the <i>Dark Cubes</i></strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Inside the Dark Cubes, conditions change quickly. Enemies alter their attack patterns and abilities from floor to floor, making every run unpredictable and if you die you start all over. Mastering the balance between your <strong>Skill Tree</strong>, <strong>Relics</strong>, and <strong>Deck composition</strong> is essential. <i>Adapt or perish</i> isn\u2019t just a phrase - it\u2019s the core of the experience. To empower players, we reintroduced the <strong>Side Deck</strong>: a strategic tool that lets you adjust your deck when needed, instead of being entirely dependent on random card rewards like in other games. It puts <strong>control back in your hands</strong> and rewards smart adaptation. But can you survive the <strong>Darkest Cube?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3650350/extras/309c4699d869fae7f8e85481effaab14.avif?t=1770890325\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>3. Co-op Mode on the Horizon</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > We believe there are too few good co-op experiences \u2014 games that truly connect and challenge friends together. In the niche of roguelike deck-builders (only around 800 titles exist), almost none explore <strong>cooperative gameplay</strong>. We want to change that. Team up with friends, face even greater challenges, and discover new <strong>synergies between decks</strong> across over <strong>60 cards per class</strong> \u2014 with <strong>five unique classes</strong> planned.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3650350/extras/262d1d4571e393b0554dfcfe9338fdaf.avif?t=1770890325\" width=800 height=450 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>4. A Draft Mode Worth Waiting For</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > We\u2019re keeping this one secret... for now. Let\u2019s just say: it will surprise you.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3650350?t=1770890325","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3650350/c388f1354fef415167ef66284ea576f060223d87/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1770890325","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3650350/2dcbb9df129547b8dd09512442472a0c9b48c34c/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1770890325","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3650350/2dcbb9df129547b8dd09512442472a0c9b48c34c/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1770890